# Fixing a Hole, verse (figure 110.2)
# Top is the vocal tune; the two middle lines carry on from the intro (fig. 110.1). Pollack leaves
# the chord row blank in mm. 3-4; m. 3 is the f chord held (his i7-), and m. 4 is his "some kind
# of Major IV" with F in the bass (IV6/4 [?]), written here as Bb/F: an addition, not typed.
# His upper middle line stops after "-" in m. 4 (no closing bar line); read as held.
# Notes in a bar get equal shares.
#? Octaves of the tune are a guess by nearest motion (F4 up to F5): check the leaps C5-F4 (m. 3) and Eb5-F4 (mm. 4-5) against the record.
#? Top line mm. 7-8 is blank in the typed chart; read as the F of "go" held.
